/-!
# Exact rational finite-Fourier bridge: actual Griess character A to C3³ torus

ORIGINAL: R. L. Griess Jr. (J. Algebra 131, 1990), Albert 27D A=(Z/3)³
fine grading. Fourier duality is standard finite Abelian representation
theory. Earlier DASHI Agda owner is
Base369PeriodicTernaryTorusPathRestrictionBidiExact; do not replace it
or identify the distinct *open* P3³ spatial graph.

F columns are 27 rational vectors indexed by lexicographic ternary sites.
Their source homogeneous coefficient at antipodal mode a is the
tau-real pair:
 phase 0 -> (1,0), phase 1 -> (0,1), phase 2 -> (-1,-1).
The source trace Gram is diag(3,(3A₂)×13).
The source character action conjugates under F to PERIODIC site
translations, not open path edges. The sum over all sites is 27*e0:
the scalar Albert UNIT corresponds to a spatial constant vector,
not to the chosen spatial origin delta-site.
No transported product/local physical Hamiltonian is asserted.
The finite native_decide equalities are SOURCE-WRITTEN and uncompiled.
-/
